<DocsLayout title="Parameter Reference - Dasher">
  <h1>Parameter Reference</h1>

  <p>This page provides a comprehensive reference for Dasher's configuration parameters.</p>

  <div class="note">
    <p><strong>Note:</strong> This reference section is under development. For the most up-to-date information, please refer to the <a href="https://github.com/dasher-project/dasher" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Dasher source code</a> and documentation.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Control Parameters</h2>

  <h3>Mouse Mode</h3>
  <p>Dasher's default control mode using a two-dimensional pointing device.</p>

  <h3>One-Dimensional Mode</h3>
  <p>Mode for users who can control only one dimension of movement.</p>

  <h3> Eyetracker Mode</h3>
  <p>Optimized dynamics for eye-tracking input devices.</p>

  <h3>Button Modes</h3>
  <p>Various modes for users who can only press buttons or switches.</p>

  <h2>Display Parameters</h2>

  <h3>Dasher Font Size</h3>
  <p>Controls the size of characters in the Dasher canvas (small, medium, large).</p>

  <h3>Edit Font Size</h3>
  <p>Controls the font size in the text box where written text appears.</p>

  <h3>Colour Scheme</h3>
  <p>Selects which colour palette file to use for rendering.</p>

  <h2>Performance Parameters</h2>

  <h3>Maximum Speed</h3>
  <p>The maximum zoom speed (1 = beginner, 4 = expert).</p>

  <h3>Auto Speed Control</h3>
  <p>When enabled, Dasher automatically adjusts speed based on user performance.</p>

  <h2>Accessibility Parameters</h2>

  <h3>Speech Output</h3>
  <p>Options for text-to-speech feedback:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Speak each word</li>
    <li>Speak on stop</li>
    <li>Control mode speaking</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Copy on Stop</h3>
  <p>Automatically copies text to clipboard when Dasher stops.</p>

  <h3>Start on Position</h3>
  <p>Allows starting Dasher by pointing at specific screen locations.</p>

  <h2>Language Model Parameters</h2>

  <h3>Training File</h3>
  <p>The text file used to train Dasher's language model.</p>

  <h3>Alphabet File</h3>
  <p>The XML file defining available characters and their order.</p>

  <h2>Advanced Parameters</h2>

  <h3>Timestamp</h3>
  <p>Enables timestamp logging for debugging.</p>

  <h3>Autocalibrate Eyetracker</h3>
  <p>Automatically corrects for eyetracker calibration drift.</p>

  <h3>Socket Interface</h3>
  <p>Enables alternative input methods via socket communication.</p>

  <div class="back-link">
    <a href="/docs/reference/">← Back to Reference</a>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>

